## DESCRIPTION
## Smooth manifolds
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Concepts for multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Smooth manifolds')

########################################################################

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "MathObjects.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

BEGIN_PGML
Let [` S = \lbrace (x,y,z) \in \mathbb{R}^3: x^2+y^2+z^2 = 1 \rbrace `] be the unit sphere. Fix [` p = (0,0,1) \in S `].

For which values of [` \epsilon `] is [` B_{\epsilon}(p) \cap S `] a graph of the form [` z = f(x,y) `] for a [` C^1 `] function [` f `]? If the answer is none, enter (0,0).

[` \epsilon \in `] ([________]{Real(0)}, [________]{Compute(sqrt(2))}).

For which values of [` \epsilon `] is [` B_{\epsilon}(p) \cap S `] a graph of the form [` y = g(x,z) `] for a [` C^1 `] function [` g `]? If the answer is none, enter (0,0).

[` \epsilon \in `] ([________]{Real(0)}, [________]{Real(0)}).

For which values of [` \epsilon `] is [` B_{\epsilon}(p) \cap S `] a graph of the form [` x = h(y,z) `] for a [` C^1 `] function [` h `]? If the answer is none, enter (0,0).

[` \epsilon \in `] ([________]{Real(0)}, [________]{Real(0)}).
END_PGML

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

ENDDOCUMENT();